Now I understand the existing behavior and tests. There's a key existing test: "head changed BUT carries its OWN red verdict — park holds" — per gh-994's I1, this behavior must CHANGE: the reset on head change must be UNCONDITIONAL ("label removal is unconditional on head change — never re-checks old state"). The ticket explicitly reframes this: "the `validation_failed` label on a PR always and only reflects the check state of the PR's current head — any head change resets the park automatically".

So gh-994 supersedes the #633 "own red verdict" guard: AC3/I1 — reset unconditional. The existing test at ~6082 ('head changed BUT carries its OWN red verdict — park holds') will need updating to the new semantics: head changed → label removed (unconditionally); the fresh red will re-park via the SET path (headChecksRed) — actually wait, the SET path re-parks in the SAME pass: after unpark, the code checks `if (!unparkedThisPass && !isMachinePrU && labelsVf.indexOf(parkLabelVf) === -1 && headChecksRed(...))` — since unparkedThisPass = true, no re-park in the same pass. Next tick: label absent, head red (guest) → re-park with new parked-head comment. Good — that's the "re-parks one CI cycle later" design.

Wait, but careful about the SET gate: `!unparkedThisPass` means a guest whose head is STILL red won't be re-parked in the same pass. Next tick it re-parks (label absent → headChecksRed → park). One-cycle delay, matches the ticket's "the fail-validation path re-parks it one CI cycle later" philosophy.

Now the design decision per the ticket:

**New first rung (gh-994): pure head-change reset.** When label present, `parkedHeadVf` (park-comment sha) known, `uHead` known, and `uHead !== parkedHeadVf` → remove label unconditionally, log `park-reset: <key> head <old>→<new>`, set unparkedThisPass = true. No actor probe, no park-time probe, no verdict probe.

This changes the existing #633 test semantics: 'head changed BUT carries its OWN red verdict — park holds' must become 'label removed unconditionally; re-park happens on a later pass'. Per the ticket: I1 says removal is unconditional on head change — never re-checks old state. Yes, this existing test pins the OLD behavior that gh-994 retracts. The ticket says "Retracted: 'the SM re-arms on label removal'..." and reframes; the "own red verdict" guard IS a re-check of old state. The ticket is the authority: AC1 — reset removes the label when heads differ. Full stop.

Also the fa #156 kicker case: machine push, head changed, parked-head comment exists → currently for machine PRs the machineUnpark rung needs probes; if probes fail → gh-952 rung needs parkedHead + verdict probe; the kicker's new head may carry a dispatched verdict 'failure'... whatever — the new first rung clears it unconditionally.

